  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A short rod of blue metal with seven rings around it, each cold to a different degree. In still weather the rings turn slowly on their own, and never all in the same direction.</p><p><strong>Chain Lightning.</strong> The rod has 7 charges and regains them all at dawn. You can expend 1 charge to cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplChainLight]{Chain Lightning} (save DC 20), or 3 charges to cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplControlWea]{Control Weather}.</p><p><strong>The Seventh Storm.</strong> Once, you can expend all 7 charges to cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplStormofVen]{Storm of Vengeance} (save DC 20). The rod then cannot do so again until seven days have passed.</p><p><strong>Storms Have Names.</strong> Each of the rod's seven storms is a storm that once happened and has a name. The wielder who learns a storm's name can ask it one question about anything that occurred beneath it, the day it broke.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
